              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "robDC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were very good. Was looking for a new recipe for Kale and found this. They are definitely spicy and the Kale cooks down quite a bit. Seems critically important to toss and coat the kale leaves evenly with the oil and spices. Note that ours were a bit salty as I overdid the salt. Probably something you want to experiment with in terms of exact seasoning amounts."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "T Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had been wanting to make crispy kale and found this recipe. It is wonderful. I love it. I did change the recipe slightly; I added a little cumin and just little garlic salt, to the chile and the sea salt. Tossed the leaves in olive oil and then really toss the seasonings on the leaves. Spread thin on a cookie plate at 400 degrees. What a tasty way to use your kale. Note: Alot of leaves dry to to a much smaller amount.",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-28T15:57:35.933Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "squeeziebrb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I baked at 350 for a total of 15 minutes, 400 seemed way too high .I reduced the amount of chili also. Very tasty snack.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-23T16:16:54.320Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
