            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cyndi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum! I didn't have chili powder and used smoked paprika instead. I served it over red rice, with a side of grilled chicken breasts. Thank you. My husband told me this recipe is now in his top three. I can't wait to try nori, like other reviews have mentioned.",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-16T21:01:52.233Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Suzanne Bleike"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good- very airy and crunchy. It would be good as a crunchy topping for a pasta dish or an appetizer. I cut back the chili spice and only lightly salted per the other reviews.",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-20T00:52:43.086Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Blancheskid"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really like these and, like a previous reviewer, think they are a bit like toasted nori. And they're low carb which is a definite plus! Since kale is so sturdy I simply used my hands to get the pieces well coated with the oil. Drizzle and then rub 'em down. I also think only 1 tsp of chili powder is sufficient, and watch the salt; it's easy to overdo it.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-06T12:17:17.677Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shawnee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was very excited to try this recipe with some leftover kale. I made the mistake of over salting...I didn't have kosher salt and just used sea salt and should have decreased the amount. Like another reviewer, I used about 1 tsp of chili powder and the flavour was great. Next time I will be more watchful during the last few minutes of cooking time since I came close to burning the whole batch--I'm looking forward to correcting my mistakes and trying this again!",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-09T17:51:08.660Z"
